---
/**
 * Homepage: the frame first (why this site exists), then the three layers
 * in build order, then benefits reorganised around who is reading, then a
 * call to carry the idea. Reuses the vision-page components so the argument
 * stays identical wherever it appears.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import UeLogo from '../assets/eu.png';
import GradientSection from '../components/GradientSection.astro';
import IconLink from '../components/IconLink.astro';
import DisplayTitle from '../components/DisplayTitle.astro';
import CardGrid from '../components/CardGrid.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import Author from '../components/Author.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import FrameIntro from '../components/vision/FrameIntro.astro';
import LayerStack from '../components/vision/LayerStack.astro';
import CrossCuttingNote from '../components/vision/CrossCuttingNote.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/vision/CallToAction.astro';
import {
  callToAction,
  crossCuttingNote,
  ctaActions,
  frameSteps,
  homeFrameIntro,
  layersSection,
  resolveLayers,
} from '../lib/vision-content';

// The frame and the layer text are shared with /vision (src/lib/vision-content.ts);
// this page renders the short form of the layers.
const layers = resolveLayers('short');
---

<Layout title="Home" description="A plan for European integration through digital government, a shared working language, and robotic reindustrialization, built over the thirty working years Europe has left.">

  <Hero
    title="Design the Europe we will grow old in"
    description={[
      'Europe is aging and the pension model is running out of workers to pay for it.',
      'We have roughly thirty years of working economy left. This is a plan for how to use them.',
    ]}
    image={{ file: UeLogo.src }}
    actions={[]}
  />

  <GradientSection variant="primary" padding="md" rounded={true}>
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-center items-center space-y-6 md:space-y-0 md:space-x-10">
      <IconLink
        href="/why"
        icon="fa-solid fa-question-circle"
        class="text-xl hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors"
        ariaLabel="Learn why EU needs reform"
      >
        Why EU Needs Reform?
      </IconLink>

      <IconLink
        href="/benefits"
        icon="fa-solid fa-globe"
        class="text-xl hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors"
        ariaLabel="See benefits for your country"
      >
        Benefits For Your Country
      </IconLink>

      <IconLink
        href="/vision"
        icon="fa-solid fa-book"
        class="text-xl hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors"
        ariaLabel="See the full vision overview"
      >
        Full Vision Overview
      </IconLink>
    </div>
  </GradientSection>

  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 my-16">
    <FrameIntro
      as="h2"
      eyebrow={homeFrameIntro.eyebrow}
      title={homeFrameIntro.title}
      steps={frameSteps}
      conclusion={homeFrameIntro.conclusion}
    />

    <div class="text-center">
      <Button href="/book/designing-our-retirement" variant="primary" size="lg">
        Read the full argument
        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right ml-2"></i>
      </Button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-10 mb-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <DisplayTitle level={2} class="text-center">{layersSection.title}</DisplayTitle>
      <p class="section-lead text-xl leading-relaxed mt-4 mb-16 text-center max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        {layersSection.lead}
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem] gap-8 items-start">
        <LayerStack layers={layers} />
        <CrossCuttingNote
          eyebrow={crossCuttingNote.eyebrow}
          title={crossCuttingNote.title}
          paragraphs={crossCuttingNote.paragraphs}
          principles={crossCuttingNote.principles}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-10 mb-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <DisplayTitle level={2}>Who this is for</DisplayTitle>
      <p class="section-lead text-xl leading-relaxed mt-4 mb-12 max-w-4xl">
        The plan only works if the people who benefit are also the people who build it.
      </p>

      <CardGrid columns={3} gap="1.5rem">
        <Card
          title="For citizens and retirees-to-be"
          color="blue"
          icon="👨‍👩‍👧‍👦"
          variant="gradient"
          href="/why"
          linkText="Why reforms are needed"
        >
          A pension system with fewer workers behind it needs a plan, not a hope. Automation is the only realistic way to keep it solvent without asking families to have more children than they choose to.
        </Card>

        <Card
          title="For engineers and business"
          color="indigo"
          icon="⚙️"
          variant="gradient"
          href="/book/robotic-reindustrialisation"
          linkText="Read the robotics proposal"
        >
          Cheap, open, hard-to-monopolise robots are a market Europe does not yet own. Building them, and the digital state that runs on a common language, is decades of engineering work worth doing.
        </Card>

        <Card
          title="For regions and member states"
          color="green"
          icon="🇪🇺"
          variant="gradient"
          href="/benefits"
          linkText="See benefits by country"
        >
          Every member state gains something different from a shared language, a digital state, and robotic production — from industrial leadership to labour mobility to border security.
        </Card>
      </CardGrid>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-10 mb-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <DisplayTitle level={2}>Common Questions</DisplayTitle>
      <FAQ
        color="indigo"
        items={[
          {
            question: 'Why do we need yet another European integration project?',
            answer: "This vision addresses today's multipolar world challenges, focusing on strategic independence and economic efficiency. Without a new cooperation framework, Europe risks internal economic conflicts and external manipulation. We need a practical approach to keep Europe competitive and united.",
          },
          {
            question: "Isn't English as a second language unfair to non-English speaking countries?",
            answer: 'A common language allows us to function as one economic entity. It enables European-scale companies and eliminates translation barriers for goods, services, and contracts. Embracing English — already the language of innovation and commerce — creates a unified economic space while preserving national languages and identities.',
          },
          {
            question: 'How will these changes benefit ordinary citizens?',
            answer: 'Citizens gain EU-wide digital healthcare with predictive analytics, universal e-learning platforms, and streamlined administration. The digital infrastructure we build will support a future economy with robotized retirement solutions as populations age. This creates a Europe with fewer bureaucratic obstacles and greater opportunities.',
          },
          {
            question: "What if Germany or other powerful countries don't agree?",
            answer: 'The initiative could begin as a project among a smaller group of willing member states. The voluntary model allows countries to join when the benefits become apparent, while creating pressure on those who remain outside.',
          },
          {
            question: 'How would this be funded?',
            answer: "We've already mobilized enormous resources for COVID-19 and security challenges. The issue isn't funding capacity but directing funds wisely. Centralizing digital development saves costs across 27 countries, and strategic borrowing for high-return projects creates self-sustaining improvements.",
          },
          {
            question: 'How long would implementation take?',
            answer: 'English language adoption can start now with formal agreements. Robotization and AI projects should launch immediately, both for defense and for the civilian capabilities they build. Rather than waiting for perfect conditions, we should adopt these reforms while they still have thirty years to pay off.',
          },
          {
            question: 'What are the main challenges, and what could go wrong?',
            answer: 'Three things, honestly. Governments may patch the demographic hole with mass immigration because it is the reflex, at a cost we do not need to pay. Treaty change needs unanimity, so the plan has to be built so that every member state wins — and it still has to survive resistance from whoever benefits from the status quo. And the gains from automation may land narrowly: if robots are expensive and easy to monopolise, we solve production and lose the distribution that made it worth solving. The worst outcome is none of these in particular — it is that nobody prepares, retirement arrives, and the money buys nothing because the system still assumes workers who no longer exist.',
          },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-10 mb-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <DisplayTitle level={2}>About the Author</DisplayTitle>
      <Author color="purple" />
    </div>

    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mt-10">
      <DisplayTitle level={2}>Stay Updated</DisplayTitle>
      <Newsletter />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-16">
    <CallToAction
      title={callToAction.title}
      paragraphs={callToAction.paragraphs}
      actions={ctaActions}
    />
  </div>

</Layout>

<style>
  .section-lead {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
